Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:09:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: Fill SIMD groups when emulating tessellation

The tessellator kernels ran one patch per threadgroup and the TCS one
patch per threadgroup of its output vertices, so a SIMD group of 32
lanes worked on one patch with one to four lanes busy. The tessellator
now runs 64 patches per threadgroup, and the TCS as many patches as fit
32 lanes, its patch and invocation IDs computed from the packed group.

Indirect draws dispatched the VS and TCS grids as threadgroup counts of
vertices and TCS invocations, 64 and output-patch-size times too many
threads, the TCS ones reading and writing past the patches. They are
thread counts with a threadgroup size now.

Rise of the Tomb Raider's benchmark, Spine of the Mountain, which
tessellates the snow, warm caches, alternating runs with cooldowns:
30.6 and 30.8 fps instead of 29.2 and 28.9, 29.9 and 30.2 with only the
TCS packed. Without the game's tessellation it runs at 38 fps.

Generated-by: LLM
